  "title": "Real-time access requests and faster approvals for content access requests",
  "product": "Confluence",
  "status": "released",
  "description": "We’re introducing real-time access requests in Confluence. If you can manage access for a content, you’ll now be able to quickly approve or deny requests if you’re active on the content through a flag, without interrupting your workflow. To respond to content access requests in real time: Open any Confluence content type (such as a published page, live doc, or whiteboard) that you can manage permissions for.\n\tIf someone requests access while you’re viewing or editing, a flag will appear on your ",
